+        # Context, not justification: unpatched cost is ~4-12 s/batch wall clock => 12-35
+        # days at min_epochs=100 with the GPU idle. (An earlier note here said 124 days; that
+        # came from tqdm's CUMULATIVE average read over the first eight batches and was an
+        # overstatement of 4-10x.)
+        # Equivalence: output bit-identical on sampled windows; loss-trajectory and per-step
+        # timing recorded in docs/acceptance/ (NOT yet run when this line was written).
+        # Scope: WindowDataset only. BinDataset still receives a DataFrame and needs one
+        # (bin_maker.py:38 calls .rolling()), so it stays bit-identical to shipped.
+        self.frames = self._scale_data(self.frames).values
 
